            <ArticleTitle>Manual handling and the elderly: a matter of restraint?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-1, 44-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 1995 nurses at Rozelle Hospital began a project to identify and record manual handling incidents at their hospital. This activity was a preliminary part of a long term project to reduce the number of injuries and sick leave resulting from manual handling. Tony Cornwell, of Rozelle Hospital, documents their findings here.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
